{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/pulls/54649","id":3833101459,"node_id":"PR_kwDOA9BSs87keHyT","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54649","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54649.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54649.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/issues/54649","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/pulls/54649/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/pulls/54649/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/issues/54649/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/statuses/658ef90a8642734370e49446fcdb1244d5a84aa5","number":54649,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[StaticWebAssets] Clear AssetGroups when materializing framework assets (fixes Blazor WASM blazor.webassembly.js 404)","user":{"login":"lewing","id":24063,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24063?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing","html_url":"https://github.com/lewing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lewing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"> [!NOTE]\n> This pull request was created with the assistance of GitHub Copilot. The root-cause analysis and fix were verified locally (see \"Verification\" below).\n\n## Summary\n\nBlazor WebAssembly apps built with the .NET 11 **Preview 6** SDK band fail to boot: the browser requests `_framework/blazor.webassembly.<fingerprint>.js` and gets **HTTP 404**, so Blazor never starts. (`dotnet.<fingerprint>.js` from the runtime pack serves fine — only `blazor.webassembly.js` 404s.)\n\n## Root cause\n\n`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly` started shipping `blazor.webassembly.js` as a **grouped Framework static web asset** (group `BlazorWebAssembly`) via aspnetcore [#66412](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/66412), using the new JSON package-assets manifest format.\n\nThis is a **missed call site from [#54049](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54049)**. That PR introduced the shared `StaticWebAsset.MaterializeFrameworkAsset` helper — which clears `AssetGroups` and normalizes the asset — to standardize how framework assets are materialized when they cross into the consuming project. It wired that helper into two of the three materialization paths:\n\n- `UpdatePackageStaticWebAssets` (old-format NuGet package path) ✅\n- `UpdateExternallyDefinedStaticWebAssets` (P2P path) ✅\n- `ReadPackageAssetsManifest` (the **new** net11 JSON-manifest NuGet path, added in [#53187](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53187)) ❌ — still used its **own private copy** of the materialization logic, which did **not** clear `AssetGroups`.\n\nAs a result, when a Blazor app consumes the net11 `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly` package, `blazor.webassembly.js` is materialized but keeps `AssetGroups = BlazorWebAssembly=enabled` after being promoted to a current-project asset. Endpoint generation then skips it as a still-grouped asset, the fingerprinted endpoint is never registered, and the browser gets a 404.\n\n## Fix\n\nComplete [#54049](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54049) by delegating `ReadPackageAssetsManifest`'s framework-asset materialization to the same shared `StaticWebAsset.MaterializeFrameworkAsset`, so all three consumption paths transform framework assets identically. This clears `AssetGroups`, normalizes the asset, removes the duplicated logic that drifted, and drops the now-dead `sourceId`/`fxDir` plumbing.\n\nA focused regression test asserts that a grouped framework asset has its `AssetGroups` cleared after materialization.\n\n## Impact / severity\n\n- Regressed in the **Preview 6** SDK band (the first band carrying aspnetcore #66412). Preview 5 is unaffected (it shipped `blazor.webassembly.js` via the old, ungrouped mechanism).\n- Affects **all** Blazor WebAssembly apps built with the affected SDK, not just internal tests. There is no workaround in app code.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced the 404 by building a `blazorwasm` template app with the affected SDK: the produced `*.staticwebassets.endpoints.json` contained **zero** `blazor.webassembly.js` (non-map) endpoints, while the source package manifest correctly defined `_framework/blazor.webassembly.<hash>.js`.\n- With this fix, the materialized asset's `AssetGroups` is empty and the endpoints reappear, including the exact `blazor.webassembly.<hash>.js` route that previously 404'd.\n- `ReadPackageAssetsManifestTest` passes (14/14), including the new regression test.\n","labels":[{"id":2671487562,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjcxNDg3NTYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/labels/Area-AspNetCore","name":"Area-AspNetCore","description":"RazorSDK, BlazorWebAssemblySDK, StaticWebAssetsSDK","color":"4A380A","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":16026691,"node_id":"MI_kwDOA9BSs84A9IxD","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/milestones/123","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/milestone/123","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/sdk/milestones/123/labels","number":123,"state":"open","title":"11.0-preview6","description":null,"creator":{"login":"dotnet-milestone-bot[bot]","id":286398033,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOERIWUQ","avatar_ur